{"paper": "2024-Tier1-12-Sep-2024-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "20% p.a.", "added": false}, {"text": "18% p.a.", "added": false}, {"text": "17% p.a.", "added": false}, {"text": "19% p.a.", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "Every month, a man consumes 20 kg of rice and 8 kg of wheat. The price of rice is 20% of the price of wheat, resulting in a total expenditure of ₹300 per month for rice and wheat combined. If the price of wheat is increased by 20%, what percentage reduction in rice consumption is needed to maintain the same expenditure of ₹300? (Given that price of rice and consumption of wheat is constant.)", "options": [{"text": "40%", "added": false}, {"text": "38%", "added": false}, {"text": "24%", "added": false}, {"text": "22%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "A thief pursued by a policeman was 150 m ahead at the start. If the ratio of the speed of the policeman to that of the thief was 5 : 4, then how far (distance in metres) could the thief go before he is caught by the policeman?", "options": [{"text": "350", "added": false}, {"text": "200", "added": false}, {"text": "600", "added": false}, {"text": "400", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "9 : 5", "added": false}, {"text": "12 : 5", "added": false}, {"text": "1 : 2", "added": false}, {"text": "5 : 12", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "81", "added": false}, {"text": "27.1", "added": false}, {"text": "63", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "Find the area of a sector with an arc length of 44 cm, which subtends a central angle of 30°.", "options": [{"text": "1488 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "1584 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "1848 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "1884 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "The following pie chart shows the study time of different subjects of a student in a day. Study the pie chart and answer the question. If the student studied English for 3 hours, then he studied Mathematics for:", "options": [{"text": "2 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "1 hour", "added": false}, {"text": "7 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "5 hours", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "Two cylinders have the radii of their bases in the ratio 4 : 5 and their heights are in the ratio 5 : 7. Find the ratio of their curved surface areas.", "options": [{"text": "5 : 4", "added": false}, {"text": "4 : 7", "added": false}, {"text": "1 : 2", "added": false}, {"text": "4 : 5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "Solve the following:", "options": [{"text": "2cosec2θ", "added": false}, {"text": "2sin2θ", "added": false}, {"text": "2sec2θ", "added": false}, {"text": "2tan2θ", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "Two pipes A and B can fill a tank in 48 minutes and 66 minutes, respectively. If both the pipes are opened simultaneously, then after how many minutes should pipe B be closed so that the tank gets filled in 32 minutes?", "options": [{"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "22", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "combined-pipes", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "3,10,000", "added": false}, {"text": "4,50,000", "added": false}, {"text": "5,00,000", "added": false}, {"text": "4,10,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "The given pie-chart shows the percentage distribution of 20,000 employees in a company. Study the given chart and answer the question that follows. If 30% of the employees in department D are females, then how many male employees are there in that department?", "options": [{"text": "4200", "added": false}, {"text": "4500", "added": false}, {"text": "5000", "added": false}, {"text": "4000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "In triangle ABC, the length of side BC is 2 cm less than twice the length of side AB. The length of side AC exceeds the length of side AB by 10 cm. The perimeter of the triangle is 40 cm. Determine the length (in cm) of the smallest side of the triangle.", "options": [{"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "The average of the squares of the first 46 natural numbers is", "options": [{"text": "729.5", "added": false}, {"text": "728.5", "added": false}, {"text": "727.5", "added": false}, {"text": "730.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "series-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "For the following equations, what are the values of a and b to have infinitely many solutions? ax + by = 2 3x - (5 - 2a)y = 6", "options": [{"text": "a = - 1,b = - 1", "added": false}, {"text": "a = - 1,b = 1", "added": false}, {"text": "a = 1,b = - 1", "added": false}, {"text": "a = 1,b = 1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "Which of following numbers is NOT divisible by 11?", "options": [{"text": "109153", "added": false}, {"text": "5445", "added": false}, {"text": "128041", "added": false}, {"text": "80124", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "576", "added": false}, {"text": "320", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "In ΔDEF, the bisector of ∠ D intersects side EF at point N. If DE = 36 cm, DF = 40 cm and EF = 38 cm, then the length (in cm) of NF is ________.", "options": [{"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "The ratio between male and female members in a club is 2 : 3. If the number of male members is increased by 200, the ratio becomes 5 : 6. How many female members are there in the club?", "options": [{"text": "1200", "added": false}, {"text": "900", "added": false}, {"text": "1400", "added": false}, {"text": "1000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "The MP of an article was Rs.180 and it was sold at a discount of 15%, the discount in Rs. is:", "options": [{"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "In a garden, there are 6 daisy plants the first year. Each year, a gardener adds 3 new daisy plants. He has 26 jasmine plants the first year and loses 2 each year. When will the number of daisy plants equal to the number of jasmine plants after the first year?", "options": [{"text": "5 years", "added": false}, {"text": "4 years", "added": false}, {"text": "2 years", "added": false}, {"text": "6 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Sequences and Series", "sub": "arithmetic-progression", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "From a point T, the length of the tangent to a circle is 32 cm and the distance of T from the centre is 40 cm. The diameter (in cm) of the circle is:", "options": [{"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "32", "added": false}, {"text": "48", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}]}